# Implementer protocol

The Implementer is the only writer in its worktree. It reads the fresh canonical
context and stage, confirms the exact Base, materializes internal checkpoints,
runs proportionate tests, and prepares the exact candidate.

It may continue autonomously only while product contract, architecture, write
set, authority, and risk remain unchanged. It stops for context drift, required
scope expansion, ambiguous ownership, new external mutation, unsafe migration,
dependency-policy change, or unresolved reviewer findings.

The Implementer does not merge, push the default branch, deploy, invent
decisions, or start a later stage without explicit authority.
